ue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Viewing a listing owned by another seller (prod-2, \\\"Vintage Denim Jacket - Size M\\\", owned by Marcus Chen) as Emma Green shows only buyer actions \\\"Add to Cart\\\" / \\\"Message Seller\\\" — no \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\" or any edit/delete controls, unlike the owner view which exposes \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\". No edit UI is exposed for non-owned listings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Create Listing\\\" with all required fields (Title, Description, Price, Category, Condition) empty did not create a listing; page remained on /create-listing and focus moved to the required Title field, blocking submission.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Entering price \\\"-50\\\" and clicking \\\"Create Listing\\\" did not submit the form; the price input has min=\\\"0\\\" and its native validity message reads \\\"Value must be greater than or equal to 0.\\\", blocking negative price submission.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No duplicate-account error feedback; success feedback shown instead\", \"actual\": \"Submitting a duplicate-email registration produced a success toast (\\\"Account created successfully!\\\") rather than any error/warning feedback, because the app does not detect duplicates.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typed \\\"lamp\\\" into the search box (character-by-character) and the item count/grid updated immediately to reflect matches without any submit button, page reload, or explicit trigger. Same instant update behavior observed for a non-matching search term (immediately switched to \\\"No items found\\\" state).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All filter/so